## MITIGATION ARGUMENT TEST

The primary mitigation argument is: "H2 revenue ramp will be achieved through subassembly automation unlocking full line capacity, combined with normalization of pricing to backlog averages."

**Sub-test 1 — SPECIFICITY:** The argument is concrete and testable. Management specifies: subassembly automation coming online in Q3/Q4, targeting CM-positive cubes in Q4, gross margin positive exiting Q1 2026, and the doubling-of-production trajectory as the bridge to guidance. Specific milestones exist against which to measure. **PASS.**

**Sub-test 2 — CAPABILITY TRACK RECORD:** The transcript provides same-transcript historical evidence: the company has doubled production output in each of the prior three quarters ("doubling output in the factory over the prior 3 quarters") using the same processes, labor, and supply chain. The subassembly automation is new, but the underlying production scaling capability has a demonstrated three-quarter track record within this transcript. The 64% improvement in part flatness and 3%+ energy efficiency improvement from early automation output are measurable early results. **PASS.**

**Sub-test 3 — CURRENT TRACTION:** The first subassembly station is installed and producing. Management reports measurable output: 64% improvement in part flatness, 3%+ energy efficiency improvement in batteries built from automated parts, and higher process capability scores. This is not just intent — there is measurable early-stage traction. **PASS.**

**Score: 3/3 passes → strong.**

