## FRESH MONEY TEST
**Fresh money allocation: 5%**

The gap between 5% (fresh money) and 8% (recommended max) reflects the following: an existing holder has already absorbed the binary risk of the H2 ramp and has a cost basis that may reflect prior uncertainty. A fresh buyer today is paying into a stock that has already risen 35% (per the mark-to-market disclosure) and is buying ahead of the largest execution test in the company's history. The 3-point gap is not inertia — it reflects that the H2 ramp is a near-term binary event, and a fresh buyer has the option to wait one quarter for confirmation at modest opportunity cost. If Q3 confirms the doubling trajectory, the fresh money allocation rises to match the 8% recommended size.

